ocean-walker is an Ocean OS port of the filesystem walker and scan-cache
implementation from Oh My Pi (OMP), used under the MIT License.

Upstream repository: https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi
Pinned revision: 03c48d073bd4849726cc14750b5aecfa310bdf26
Donor source paths:
  crates/pi-walker/src/lib.rs
  crates/pi-walker/src/cache.rs
Donor test paths:
  crates/pi-walker/tests/parallel.rs
  crates/pi-walker/tests/perf.rs

Source and deterministic tests were adapted for Ocean-native crate, thread,
temporary-path, documentation, and OCEAN_WALK_WORKERS names, and for Rust 2021
syntax at Ocean's Rust 1.88 MSRV. The ignored deterministic performance harness
is retained but is not part of ordinary test runs because it creates more than
15,000 files and is intended for explicit single-threaded measurement.

